course: dictionary
lesson: 3893
title: Freshwater
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Freshwater is water that is not salty. Rivers, lakes, ponds and streams are freshwater, while the sea is salt water. Freshwater is the opposite of saltwater, so if you know one word, you can work out the other.
explain: The word has two parts, fresh and water. «Freshwater mussels filter and clean river water as they feed» tells you the mussels live in a river, where the water is not salty. Look for clues like river, lake or pond, because they often show the water is freshwater.
explain: Watch out for the two-word form, fresh water. It is a noun, meaning water that people, animals and plants can drink or use. In «The village needs more fresh water», the water itself is the thing being talked about. In «a freshwater lake», the word describes the lake. Check the sentence to see which one fits.
fact: Freshwater describes water that is not salty, like the water in rivers, lakes, ponds and streams.
fact: «Lake Superior» is the largest freshwater lake by area, at about 82,000 square kilometres.
fact: «The Mekong giant catfish» is one of the biggest freshwater fish, and it is now very rare.
fact: Only a tiny part of the water on Earth is fresh, and much of that is frozen in ice caps and glaciers, so we must save water.
fact: Scientists sort habitats into freshwater (ponds, rivers, lakes) and marine (the sea).
exercise: «Freshwater mussels filter and clean river water as they feed.» Where do these mussels live? | In the sea | *In a river | In a desert | In a salt mine
exercise: What does freshwater mean? | Water with salt in it | *Water that is not salty | Water that is always frozen | Water from the sea
exercise: «The Mekong giant catfish is one of the biggest freshwater fish.» Which word tells you the fish lives in water that is not salty? | catfish | one | biggest | *freshwater
test: Which is a freshwater habitat? | Ocean | Coral reef | *Lake | Open sea
test: «The village needs more fresh water.» What does fresh water mean here? | A cold wind | Water with lots of salt in it | Water that is frozen solid | *Water without salt that people can drink or use
exam: Which sentence uses freshwater as an adjective? | Fresh water is needed for drinking | *The ponds are home to freshwater fish | Salt water is found in the sea | The fish swam quickly
